48	// Undo / redo.
49	//
50	// There is exactly one restorable state in this product: a successful build's
51	// `filesSnapshot`. Nothing else is versioned — a Brand or SEO save overwrites
52	// the draft files in place, and no route can write an arbitrary tree back. So
53	// undo is defined over CHECKPOINTS, and this comment is the honest statement of
54	// what that does and does not give you:
55	//
56	//   * Undoing a build restores the checkpoint before it.
57	//   * Undoing a manual edit (Brand / SEO) restores the checkpoint it was made
58	//     on top of — so the edit is undone, but as a side effect of putting the
59	//     whole tree back, not because the edit itself was recorded.
60	//   * A manual edit therefore CANNOT BE REDONE. Nothing captured it. Redo says
61	//     so rather than offering a button that would silently do something else.
62	//
63	// `cursor` is the checkpoint the draft matches. Within a session it is a fact:
64	// every move is one this component performed itself. Across a reload it is
65	// seeded from an exact server-side tree comparison (page.tsx) that can answer
66	// only one question — "does the draft match the NEWEST checkpoint?" — because
67	// answering it for every checkpoint would mean loading every snapshot.
68	//
69	// So a reloaded page knows either "the draft is at the newest checkpoint" or
70	// "the draft is somewhere else", and NOT where else. That is why the
71	// off-checkpoint label says "restore the last build" rather than "go back":
72	// after a restore-then-reload the newest checkpoint is forwards, not
73	// backwards, and a button claiming otherwise would be wrong. Restoring the
74	// last build is a true description of the click in both cases.
75	//
76	// A checkpoint can also vanish underneath all of this: lib/retention.ts clears
77	// old snapshots, and the checkpoint list only ever contains surviving ones. So
78	// every target is re-checked at click time and a 404 is reported as what it is.
79	// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
