7	// Version history. Every row is a real, restorable checkpoint — a successful
8	// build whose `filesSnapshot` still exists.
9	//
10	// TWO TRUTHS THIS PANEL HAS TO CARRY, because getting either wrong turns a
11	// safety net into a trap:
12	//
13	//  1. HISTORY IS BOUNDED. lib/retention.ts clears `filesSnapshot` on any build
14	//     that is BOTH past the newest 20 for its project AND older than 30 days
15	//     (SNAPSHOT_KEEP_PER_PROJECT = 20, SNAPSHOT_MIN_AGE_DAYS = 30). Both the
16	//     server list route and page.tsx filter on the snapshot surviving, so a
17	//     cleared checkpoint stops appearing rather than sitting here as a row
18	//     that 404s when clicked. The footnote says so out loud, because "my
19	//     history only goes back so far" is otherwise discovered as a bug.
20	//  2. RESTORING IS NOT A REFUND. It writes an old tree back over the draft.
21	//     It does not cancel the build it steps over, does not return its credits
22	//     and does not un-publish anything. It is itself free — see the restore
23	//     route — and that is a different claim.
24	//
25	// WHAT IS NOT HERE, because it does not exist: an arbitrary A-vs-B compare.
26	// loadBuildDiff() answers exactly one question — what did THIS build change
27	// against the newest earlier surviving checkpoint — so "Compare" is offered as
28	// that, and DiffView names the checkpoint it compared against.
29	
30	export type BuildCheckpoint = {
31	  id: string;
32	  prompt: string;
33	  createdAt: string;
34	  filesWritten: number;
35	};
